<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Nov 23.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Nov 23.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended Nov 23</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   155	   0.17     493550  76.50     5.72</p>
<p>State Bank	   215	   0.22     309850  66.62     5.34</p>
<p>ACC		   1120	   1.16	26660  29.86     5.40</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    350	   0.29	78700  27.55     4.32</p>
<p>Tata Power	   109	   0.13     172900  18.85     6.22</p>
<p>MTNL		   215	   0.04	38600   8.30     0.25</p>
<p>IPCL		   101	   0.00	79300   8.01     0.00</p>
<p>ICICI		   53	   0.03     142500   7.55     2.95</p>
<p>Andhra Valley	 95	   0.13	65650   6.24     7.14</p>
<p>Arvind Mills	 109	   0.12	52100   5.68     5.74</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 4.96 percent on an annualised basis against 6.75 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Nov 16. The average badla charge takes into account the book-closure badla charges.</p>
<p>The following scrip has gone into book-closure- MTNL.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
